Ladybird keeps ticking effects with finite end times in box-less
iframes. A zero-duration effect has zero active duration even with
infinite iterations, so its end delay can still produce a finite end.

Blink uses Animation::UpdateFinishedState() to compare the current time
with EffectEnd(). Gecko uses Animation::UpdateFinishedState() and
EffectEnd() for the same decision. WebKit checks effectEndTime() in
WebAnimation::updateFinishedState(). Ladybird follows their completion
rule by retaining normal ticks for these effects.
